// endpoint_set_workspace_principal_link.proto — SetWorkspacePrincipalLink:
// name the one link that best stands for a workspace's task, or clear it.
// AGENT API section.
//
// THE PRINCIPAL LINK IS THE TOPBAR SUMMARY'S DESTINATION. While one is set,
// the topbar draws the workspace's summary as a link to it
// (frontend.v1.TopbarTitle.link), and a click opens it the way every outward
// link opens: OpenExternal, in the Chrome profile of the account the
// workspace's session spends as. A workspace with no summary draws nothing
// clickable, whatever its link.
//
// THE AGENT KEEPS IT CURRENT. An agent sets it, without asking anyone, when a
// link supplied in its conversation best reflects the workspace's current
// summary or task (a pull request, a ticket, a design doc), and replaces it
// when a more fitting one arrives. Setting a workspace's link replaces the
// one it had; there is only ever one.
//
// DURABLE: the daemon records the link on the workspace, so it stands across
// a daemon restart, and every set and clear republishes the workspace's
// topbar. GetWorkspaceStatus reads it back (WorkspaceStatus.principal_link).

